# Cell from playpick: mode=raid, boss=confluence (The Confluence),
# spec=druid:restoration, style=mash, size=10, difficulty=normal,
# view=390x844,touch, save=fresh.
#
# First true mode=raid pull of The Confluence this job has ever run. The one
# prior appearance of this boss id (2026-09-25, mode=daily, druid:balance,
# good/idle/mash comparison) never actually landed on Confluence -- playpick's
# boss label for a daily is unreachable and the real daily that day turned out
# to be The Two Flasks. So every number below is the first this job has on
# this specific fight.
#
# Worth playing carefully because docs/upkeep.md's own "raid rewarding play"
# table has Confluence at played=72%/idle=18%, a +54 gap in playing's favour --
# the opposite direction from every entry direction.md's line 1 has found so
# far, and the second-largest gap on the whole table after Skyward Deck and
# Long Cold. Read src/sim/boss.ts's confluence section first (per
# docs/reading-the-source.md's spirit -- know what a fight asks before playing
# it): its own comment says this is "the one boss on this roster whose demand
# is not about where the raid is standing... it asks about the geometry
# between the fight's own bodies" -- an infection/ooze mark that must not be
# allowed to end up near another one, never placed on the tank, never twice on
# the same body. mash reacts to countdown telegraphs but does not deliberately
# separate marked bodies from each other, so this cell is also a look at
# whether a style with no explicit "keep marks apart" logic can still clear a
# fight built specifically to ask that question.
#
# The boss is index 4 in src/sim/encounters.ts, well past a fresh save's
# default unlock (Bonegrinder 10N only per #273), so reached the documented
# way: an invite hash unlocks the tier it names and everything below it.
open #b=confluence&s=10&h=0
tap class:druid:restoration
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot open

play mash 130
bill
state
shot mid1

play mash 130
bill
state
says
shot end
